In the most recent preparation of this index, completed in 2023, India secured the eighth position. This shift in India's standing may be attributed to a decline in the occurrence of disasters or the nation's ongoing enhancement of its resilience.

The report, developed through an analysis of current and past climate data, was unveiled on the second day of the ongoing COP30 climate summit taking place in Belém, Brazil.
