Authorities announced on Tuesday that the death toll from a week of flooding and unprecedented rainfall in central Vietnam had climbed to 40. The region has been submerged by relentless downpours, transforming streets into waterways, overflowing riverbanks, and flooding several of the nation's most frequented historic landmarks, as reported by the environment ministry’s disaster management agency.

