Firefighters have retrieved the remains of two victims following a massive mudslide that engulfed three homes in Brazzano di Cormons, near Gorizia, during the night spanning Sunday to Monday. The bodies of 83-year-old Guerrina Skocaj and 32-year-old Quirin Kuhnert, a German man, were recovered. Authorities retrieved Skocaj's remains overnight, following the discovery of Kuhnert's body earlier on Monday. Kuhnert tragically lost his life in an effort to save Skocaj from her home, recognizing the impending landslide triggered by severe torrential rain.

The entire region has transformed into a massive heap of debris. Rescuers successfully extracted a single individual from the debris, still alive, who sustained a leg fracture and was transported to a medical facility in Udine.

Severe weather conditions similarly led to flooding, destruction, and significant disruptions across various regions of Friuli Venezia Giulia, prompting the declaration of a regional state of emergency.

