A massive mudslide in Brazzano di Cormons, near Gorizia, demolished three homes and claimed two lives between Sunday night and Monday morning. Firefighters retrieved the bodies of 32-year-old German Quirin Kuhnert and 83-year-old Guerrina Skocaj. Kuhnert's body was discovered on Monday, while Skocaj's was located overnight.

Kuhnert valiantly lost his life attempting to rescue Skocaj from her residence after recognizing the impending landslide, which was triggered by a deluge of heavy rainfall that had struck the town. One survivor was successfully extracted from the wreckage, sustaining a broken leg, and was transported to a hospital in Udine. The area now stands as an immense heap of debris.

This incident is part of broader severe weather events that have led to flooding, destruction, and significant disturbances across various areas of Friuli Venezia Giulia. A regional state of emergency has been declared for Friuli Venezia Giulia, along with other affected regions.

